            <h1>Expensive coaching vs skill building: which is better for your child?</h1>
            <p class="line strong">
              Expensive coaching vs skill building which is better for child comes down to one honest question most families skip: what is the money actually buying? A shot at one specific exam, or a broader skill portfolio that pays off either way? Coaching earns its cost only when your child is chasing a genuinely exam-gated outcome, like a licensed medical seat through NEET. For almost everything else — general employability, income growth, staying relevant as AI reshapes entry-level work — skill building backed by real proof of work is the stronger bet per rupee spent. The right skill portfolio is what actually unlocks high income opportunities and moves a child toward earlier financial freedom. And unlike a single exam bet, it does not evaporate to zero if one exam day goes badly.
            </p>

            <div class="key-takeaways">
              <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Top-tier JEE/NEET coaching in Kota runs Rs 75,000-1.8 lakh a year in tuition alone; add hostel, food, and travel and the real cost is Rs 2-3.5 lakh a year — and 40-50% of NEET registrants each year are repeat candidates paying that cost twice or more.</li>
                <li>JEE Advanced's qualifying rate sits near 30% of those who already cleared JEE Main; NEET has roughly 1.2 million qualifiers chasing about 1.3 lakh government MBBS seats nationally — coaching improves odds, it does not guarantee the seat.</li>
