                <li>82% of Indian employers report difficulty finding candidates with the right practical skills, and skills-first hiring is rising — a real, unmet market exists for demonstrated skill that exam coaching alone does not build.</li>
                <li><strong>The real decision filter is not "which is better in general" — it is whether your child's goal is genuinely exam-gated, and if not, how much of the coaching budget can move toward a high-value skill portfolio that survives a bad exam result and unlocks earlier financial freedom either way.</strong></li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
